<title>JAPAN: Hanwa to sell land near Tokyo to offset bond loss.</title>
<headline>Hanwa to sell land near Tokyo to offset bond loss.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese steel wholesaler Hanwa Co Ltd said on Thursday that it will sell real estate near Tokyo to the Contruction Ministry-affliated Organisation for Promoting Urban Development for 5.6 billion yen on March 10.</p>
<p>Hanwa said in a statement that income from the land sale will offset a write-off of losses made in foreign bond investments and repayment of loans.</p>
<p>The land will be jointly developed by Hanwa and the organisation, the statement said.</p>
</text>
